Modifications: the files were modified. SKILL.md was written fresh in the
house style as one skill with four modes (write, audit, restructure,
beautify) and a facts-from-the-repo rule. references/templates.md merges
samber's skeletons by project type with softaworks' internal, personal and
config-directory templates, adds a monorepo-root router, and condenses the
section patterns. references/audit-checklist.md condenses samber's scorecard,
fix order, cold-reader test and sourced-statistics policy (enterprise steps,
interview, and traffic tracking dropped). references/badges-and-visuals.md
combines samber's badge evidence with oil-oil's hero, SVG and visual-direction
rules (ImageGen hybrid composition, GIF rendering script, showcase and
attribution offers dropped) and adds a shields.io table whose endpoints were
checked against img.shields.io. references/github-rendering.md is new, written
from the GitHub docs (README precedence, 500 KiB truncation, Outline, relative
links, <picture>, alerts, details, anchors, Mermaid, sanitised HTML).
scripts/readme_audit.sh ports samber's readme-audit.sh with fixes (links
starting with / resolve from the repo root when the README lives in .github/
or docs/; angle-bracket and HTML src/srcset/href targets are checked; only a
root README shadowed by .github/README.md is reported) and adds oil-oil's
image alt-text and SVG checks in bash. awesome-copilot's create-readme
contributed the rules on emoji restraint, GFM alerts, using an existing logo
in the header and keeping LICENSE/CONTRIBUTING/CHANGELOG content in their own
files.
